{"study_accession":"PRJNA693508","secondary_study_accession":"SRP302540","title":"Hsa_circRNA_G004213 Promotes Cisplatin Sensitivity by Regulating miR-513b-5p/PRPF39 in Liver Cancer","description":"Purpose:In recent years, increasing evidence has confirmed that exosomal circular RNAs (circRNAs) play a crucial role in the prognostic prediction and diagnosis of liver cancer （LC）. In this study, we first compared the expression patterns of exosomal circRNAs during transarterial chemoembolization (TACE). Methods:CircRNA-seq identified 390 differentially expressed circRNAs between the prior TACE and TACE1 groups and 489 differentially expressed circRNAs between the prior TACE and TACE2 groups. GO analysis of the differentially expressed circRNAs showed that they were associated with fatty acid metabolism, receptor binding and membrane protein complexes. KEGG pathway analysis predicted that protein digestion and absorption pathways were activated after TACE. And we screened out a novel gene , hsa_circRNA_G004213 (circ_G004213) was significantly upregulated after TACE (fold change >10, P<0.01). Further analysis found circ_G004213 significantly increased the cisplatin sensitivity of HepG2 cells and positively correlated with the prognosis of tumor-bearing mice. Based on the potential downstream miRNAs and mRNAs, the circRNA‐miRNA-mRNA network was constructed. Results: We demonstrated that circ_G004213 regulates cisplatin resistance via the miR-513b-5p/PRPF39 axis. Finally, our study confirmed that circ_G004213 was positively correlated with the prognosis of LC patients after TACE. Therefore, circ_G004213 may be used as an indicator for predicting the efficacy of TACE. Conclusions: Hsa_circRNA_G004213 Promotes Cisplatin Sensitivity by Regulating miR-513b-5p/PRPF39 in Liver Cancer. Overall design: We collected hepatic artery blood from 5 LC patients at three time points: prior to TACE treatment (prior TACE), after the first TACE operation (TACE1) and after the second TACE operation (TACE2). Then, the exosomes were extracted from the blood, and the alterations of the circRNAs in exosomes were further analyzed.","pubmed":"33864660","geo_series":"","n_samples":15,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17389259","study_accession":"PRJNA693508","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"11A","description":"11A","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5027807","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-01-23","attributes":[["source_name","Pre-TACE case1"],["case","1"],["tissue","hepatic artery blood"],["time","Pre-TACE"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13489933","experiment_accession":"SRX9902538","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":32922499,"base_count":9876749700,"first_public":"2021-01-23","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM5027807: 11A Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17389260","study_accession":"PRJNA693508","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"17V","description":"17V","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5027821","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-01-23","attributes":[["source_name","TACE2 case5"],["case","5"],["tissue","hepatic artery blood"],["treatment","TACE"],["time","TACE2"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13489947","experiment_accession":"SRX9902552","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":31065188,"base_count":9319556400,"first_public":"2021-01-23","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM5027821: 17V Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17389261","study_accession":"PRJNA693508","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"15V","description":"15V","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5027820","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-01-23","attributes":[["source_name","TACE2 case4"],["case","4"],["tiss